0..76 Comment "// A rule written as an equation, `<=>`: one term spelled two ways, with the"
77..155 Comment "// left side the one a reader would rewrite to. The order of terms chooses the"
156..234 Comment "// direction, so `x <=> S(P(x))` still runs `S(P(x))` to `x` (Huet, _Confluent"
235..312 Comment "// reductions_, doi:10.1145/322217.322230). The integers are named apart from"
313..372 Comment "// the base\'s, whose rules are written the other way round."
374..440 Comment "/// The integers with their first rule written smaller side first."
